{
 "schema": "terluna.atmosphere.rain-rates/1",
 "evidence": "Statistics of the GCM's output: total precipitation in 3-day and 6.5-hour means over the land of a T21 grid, weighted by land area. The targets' 3-day statistics interpolate two runs of different physics by the ground's temperature, as the climate targets do; their 6.5-hour statistics carry the design case's short weather to them by quantile ratios. Both runs take the design sunlight without the dimming a target needs; the climate targets' cut of the land's mean rain for that dimming is carried beside each target's statistics.",
 "reading_rule": "Rates are mm/h of rain at the ground, means over a T21 cell and an output window. A mean is wet at wet_threshold_mm_h or more; wet.share is the share of the land's time in wet means and wet.p10-p99 and top are the wet means' quantiles and largest, each weighted by land area. runs gives the two runs' 3-day means over years 10-19; short gives the design case's 6.5-hour years, the 3-day means their elevens make and the ratio of the first to the second at each statistic; targets gives each target's 3-day statistics, interpolated with its share_of_the_way from the climate targets (held_in: their targets, or their resort band's rows), and its 6.5-hour statistics, those times the design case's ratios. land_rain_with_the_dimmings_own_cut_mm_day is the climate targets' land rain with the dimming's own cut, [low, high], and dimmings_own_cut_percent the cut it takes from the mean, [least, most].",
 "assumptions": [
  "The land is every cell's land fraction, weighted by the cell's area, as the climate targets weigh the land's rain; the T21 grid cannot resolve the coasts.",
  "Each target between the two runs takes their statistics linear in the ground's temperature, as the climate targets take their climate; the hot world is the test run itself, the lock the design case and the resort the climate targets' candidate at 301 K, where the author set it on 18 October.",
  "The short weather is the design case's, near 295 K, over two years: the warmer targets take its ratios of 6.5-hour to 3-day rain.",
  "Both runs take the design sunlight, without the dimming the resort and the lock need. That dimming cuts the land's mean rain by dimmings_own_cut_percent in the climate targets; how the cut divides between how often and how hard it rains is open, and spread evenly over the rates it would lower each by that share.",
  "A cell's mean rain spreads a storm over 170 km and over the window: a point under a shower sees heavier, briefer rain than any of these means."
 ],
